// A wildcard import of a module that declares a macro compiles, and the folded
// macro expands in the importer beside the folded function.
//
// The fold once abandoned the compile here: it asked every named node of the
// imported module whether it was private, and asking a macro for its name
// reached a node kind the name lookup did not know, which the compiler reports
// as its own defect and exits on. So this file's assertion is that the fold
// compiles, that the macro expanded where it was used, and that the function
// is declared while the macro, which leaves no entity behind, is not.
//
// It compiles rather than runs because the imported module's bodies are never
// generated here, so there is nothing to link the call against. The symbol
// check in cases.toml carries what running it would otherwise have shown.
//
// The imported module is modulemacro.cone.

import modulemacro::*

fn imports() i64 {
  bump(four)
}
